# Runtime imports, not TYPE_CHECKING: Data/Operations carry string forward
# references to these aliases, and Data.from_xml() must be able to rebuild the
# aggregate model. Under TYPE_CHECKING the aliases do not exist at runtime and
# pydantic raised "name '_m_<module>' is not defined" on the first parse.
#
# `from . import <name>` cannot be used: if the package already has an
# attribute with that name (a YANG module named `element` or `ConfigDict`),
# importlib's fromlist handling returns the attribute instead of the submodule.
# import_module always returns the module object.
